I would like to build addition counter-example search tools. A serious candidate image should show four simultaneous properties.

### Height panel

The curve should remain banded for a long time:

[
\log_2 x_n\in [H-D,H+D]
]

with no obvious downward trend.

### Phase map

The window should sit near:

[
\text{mean letter}\approx\log_2 3
]

but with visible non-coboundary bias:

[
|D_3|,\ |D_9|,\dots \text{ nontrivial}.
]

### Complexity panel

It should have near-full factor diversity at

[
p\approx\log_2Y.
]

I would add this as a new visualization: plot

[
\frac{P_w(p)}{M-p+1}
]

against (p), with the critical scale (p=\lfloor\log_2Y\rfloor) marked.

A true surviving candidate should be close to (1) at the critical scale.

### Mixed-tower panel

It should fail to acquire a max-plus descent certificate at tested levels (2^a3^b).

This is the strongest diagnostic. If a candidate gets a certificate, it is not a counterexample; it is a descent-forcing trap.

